@node Authorship
@section Authorship

@vindex redline-author
The user option @code{redline-author} is the label written as @samp{by} on every comment, reply and suggestion you create. The default is @samp{"user"}, a string. Roughdraft labels people @samp{user} and agents @samp{AI}, so keep the default if you want files to look the same as those Roughdraft writes; set it to your name if several people review the same files. Markup that has no author when it is first given an id is labelled @samp{user}, as Roughdraft does.

@node Choosing an adapter
@section Choosing an adapter

@vindex redline-adapter-alist
The user option @code{redline-adapter-alist} chooses the adapter for a buffer. Each element is a list @samp{(MODE FEATURE VARIABLE)}: in buffers whose major mode derives from @samp{MODE}, @samp{redline} loads @samp{FEATURE} and uses the adapter stored in @samp{VARIABLE}. The default maps @code{markdown-mode} (and so @code{gfm-mode}) to @code{redline-markdown-adapter} and @code{org-mode} to @code{redline-org-adapter}. Buffers in any other mode use @code{redline-plain-adapter}. Add an entry if you write Markdown in a mode that does not derive from @code{markdown-mode}. See @ref{Adapters} for what an adapter is.

@node Display timing
@section Display timing

@vindex redline-refresh-delay
The user option @code{redline-refresh-delay} is the number of seconds of idle time after an edit before the review display is redrawn. The default is @samp{0.3}. Raise it if redrawing becomes noticeable in very long files. It affects only the display: commands always parse the buffer afresh before changing it, so a pending redraw never makes a command act on stale positions.

@node Agent hand-off
@section Agent hand-off

@vindex redline-send-function
@vindex redline-spec-url
The user option @code{redline-send-function} is the function that hands a reviewed file to an AI agent. It is called with two arguments, the file name and a prompt string. The default, @samp{nil}, makes @code{redline-send-to-agent} copy the prompt to the kill ring so that you can paste it into any agent yourself. Set it to a function that submits the prompt to your agent tool; see @ref{Working with agents} for an example.

The user option @code{redline-spec-url} is the address of the format specification quoted in that prompt. Its default is the specification in the Roughdraft repository. Change it if you keep a pinned copy.

@node Org export
@section Org export

@vindex redline-org-export-style
The user option @code{redline-org-export-style} controls what happens to CriticMarkup when an Org file is exported. Its value is a symbol:

@itemize
@item
@code{original} (the default) exports the text as it was before the suggestions: pending insertions are dropped, and deleted and replaced text is kept.
@item
@code{accepted} exports the text as if every suggestion had been accepted.
@item
@code{markup} exports the CriticMarkup unchanged.
@end itemize

The first two drop comments and the delimiters of commented passages. Use @code{accepted} to preview the document with all suggestions applied without changing the file. Literal examples inside code are never touched. See @ref{Org files}.

@node Faces
@chapter Faces

@vindex redline-highlight
@vindex redline-insertion
@vindex redline-deletion
@vindex redline-indicator
@vindex redline-resolved
Five faces style the review display. @code{redline-highlight} marks commented passages with a background. @code{redline-insertion} shows suggested insertions (and the new text of a replacement) underlined in green, and @code{redline-deletion} shows suggested deletions (and the old text of a replacement) struck through in red. @code{redline-indicator} is used for the comment indicators that stand in for hidden comments. @code{redline-resolved} dims every part of a resolved thread; it is combined with the other faces, so a resolved suggestion keeps its strike-through. The faces have separate light and dark background variants.

