@end menu

@node Parsing a buffer
@section Parsing a buffer

@findex redline-parse
@findex redline-doc
@findex redline-adapter
@code{redline-parse} takes an adapter and returns a @code{redline-doc} structure for the current buffer: its items (comments and suggestions with merged metadata), its inline tokens, its literal regions and its review block. @code{redline-doc} returns the current buffer's parse, reparsing only when the buffer has changed, and @code{redline-adapter} returns the adapter @code{redline-adapter-alist} selects for the current buffer. These are the entry points if you want to build on the review data, for example to count open threads in a mode line. Each item is a @code{redline-item} structure; an inline item also has a @code{redline-token}, which records the buffer positions of its delimiters, text and metadata.

@findex redline-thread-roots
@findex redline-item-root
@findex redline-item-children
@findex redline-item-descendants
@findex redline-item-parent-id
@findex redline-item-by-id
@findex redline-item-for-token
@findex redline-suggestion-p
@findex redline-item-resolved-p
Threads are navigated with @code{redline-thread-roots} (all roots in document order), @code{redline-item-root}, @code{redline-item-children}, @code{redline-item-descendants} and @code{redline-item-parent-id}. A comment written right after a suggestion has that suggestion as its parent, and a reply whose parent is missing or is itself is treated as a root, so traversal always terminates. @code{redline-item-by-id} and @code{redline-item-for-token} look items up, and @code{redline-suggestion-p} and @code{redline-item-resolved-p} test them.

@node Reading and writing the review block
@section Reading and writing the review block

@findex redline-endmatter-read
@findex redline-endmatter-section
@findex redline-endmatter-editable-model
@findex redline-endmatter-put
@findex redline-endmatter-delete
@findex redline-endmatter-ids
@findex redline-endmatter-entry-fields
@findex redline-endmatter-serialize
@findex redline-endmatter-scalar
@code{redline-endmatter-read} parses review YAML and returns a structure, or @samp{nil} if the YAML is not a map with a @samp{comments} or @samp{suggestions} section; @code{redline-endmatter-section} returns one section as an alist. Edits go through an editable model: @code{redline-endmatter-editable-model} returns a copy (and signals an error for a block that cannot be rewritten safely), @code{redline-endmatter-put} and @code{redline-endmatter-delete} change it, @code{redline-endmatter-ids} and @code{redline-endmatter-entry-fields} inspect it, and @code{redline-endmatter-serialize} turns it back into YAML@. @code{redline-endmatter-scalar} formats one string as a YAML scalar. Parsing uses the @samp{yaml} package, except that double-quoted strings are decoded by @samp{redline} itself because that package mishandles some backslash escapes.

@node Adapters
@section Adapters

@findex redline-adapter-create
@findex redline-merge-regions
@findex redline-region-member
An adapter is a @code{redline-adapter} structure made with @code{redline-adapter-create}. Its slots are a @samp{name}, a @samp{code-regions-function} returning sorted @samp{(BEG . END)} literal regions, an @samp{inline-literal-regexp} and @samp{inline-literal-function} for literal objects inside paragraphs (such as code spans), a @samp{boundary-regexp} for paragraph ends other than blank lines, an @samp{endmatter-locate-function} and @samp{endmatter-wrap-function} that find and build the review block, and @samp{strict-endmatter}, which applies the specification's rule that a trailing YAML block counts as review data only if the text refers to it. @code{redline-merge-regions} and @code{redline-region-member} help with region lists. To support another markup language, define an adapter and add it to @code{redline-adapter-alist}.

@findex redline-agent-prompt
@code{redline-agent-prompt} returns the hand-off prompt for a file and an adapter name, in case you want to send it some other way.

